Phase 1: Acquisition (Free)
User downloads app, enters location, performs DIY soil test (or upgrades to mail-in lab).
Cost to you: Hosting, soil-type lookup tables, weather API calls.
User value: Immediate guild candidates (no lab wait); transparency on uncertainty.
Phase 2: Guild Refinement (Freemium)
Lab results arrive; app refines guilds with actual NPK data.
Free tier: See top 3 guilds, basic water/fertilizer recommendations.
Premium tier: Full guild ranking, labor/cost breakdown, multi-year budget templates, market-price integration, herbicide risk mapping, bulk supplier directory.
Cost to you: Minimal incremental (already computed); monetization trigger.
Phase 3: Deployment & Ongoing Reporting (Data Goldmine)
User plants guild, logs observations via app: phenology photos, pest counts, yield harvest data, water inputs, labor hours, soil amendment applications.
Free: Basic yield tracking; comparison to guild baseline.
Premium: Detailed ROI dashboard, seasonal forecasting, anomaly alerts, network benchmarking (anonymized).
Cost to you: Cloud storage for observations; minimal compute.
Phase 4: Model Improvement (Academic + Product Value)
Aggregate anonymized user data (100+ sites across climate/soil zones).
Publication cycle: Annual peer-reviewed papers on model validation, guild performance, pest-control efficacy, labor efficiency.
Product loop: Retrain functions (f(water), f(pests), f(labor)) on real-world data; push updates to app.
User incentive: Co-authorship pathway for high-quality data reporters; premium tools (labor scheduling, market forecasting) funded by research grants or corporate sponsors.
Cost to you: Statistical analysis, writing, student/postdoc labor (grant-funded ideally).
Phase 5: Corporate Adoption (Scale)
Target: Agribusinesses, land trusts, conservation districts needing site-specific recommendations.
Offering: White-label guild builder + reporting dashboard; API for bulk site evaluation.
Revenue: Licensing ($per-site or per-year), data-sharing agreements, or commission on input reductions (e.g., "we saved you 40% fertilizer—take 5%").
Your cost: API maintenance, integration support.
